scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:380:    add("### MARGIN is a diagnostic, not a sealed production option")
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:383:        "No MARGIN provisioner or fading-quantile constant exists under `physics_v025`. The task-defined MARGIN calculation therefore uses the project's nearest authenticated fading quantile: elevation-specific q10 from [mechanism_corpus.py:47](src/mcrl/stagec_v025/mechanism_corpus.py#L47) and [mechanism_corpus.py:95](src/mcrl/stagec_v025/mechanism_corpus.py#L95). It is the 10th percentile of the production Rician-times-lognormal-shadow-times-deterministic-scintillation multiplier, evaluated by 192-point Gauss-Hermite quadrature and 60 bisections ([mechanism_corpus.py:53](src/mcrl/stagec_v025/mechanism_corpus.py#L53), [mechanism_corpus.py:78](src/mcrl/stagec_v025/mechanism_corpus.py#L78)). "
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:384:        f"At 30 deg, `q10={q10:.12f}`. MARGIN uses `p_req=Gamma*N_noise/(g_nom*q10)`, so a q10 fade lands on the same mode threshold. SEALED uses divisor 1."
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:391:    add("### SEALED — nominal threshold exactly (current law)")
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:393:    out.extend(d1_table("SEALED"))
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:396:        f"SEALED first hits the RF cap at n={first_cap(sealed_curve)}. Required SE first exceeds the table maximum at n=13."
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:399:    add("### MARGIN — threshold divided by elevation-specific fading q10 (diagnostic)")
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:401:    out.extend(d1_table("MARGIN"))
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:404:        f"MARGIN first hits the RF cap at n={first_cap(margin_curve)}. Required SE first exceeds the table maximum at n=13. Once capped, PA and total power remain at their cap values even though uncapped need continues to grow."
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:410:        "For partition occupancies `(n1,...,nk)`, delivered rate is `sum_b B*eta_mode(nb)` and power is `sum_b(P_PA(p_req(nb))+0.338)+0.200` W. SEALED delivery is evaluated at its nominal design point; MARGIN delivery is evaluated at the q10 fade for which it was provisioned, so each uses the target mode's production ACM capacity. All beams are packed on one active satellite, because no per-satellite beam ceiling is declared and this is the energy-minimizing placement. Infeasible occupancies (uncapped RF above 1.65 W or no ACM mode) are excluded because all N users must be served. EE is delivered bit/s divided by watts, i.e. bit/J."
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:416:        "This is an interior solution for both rules. The unconstrained one-beam efficiency curve peaks at n=7 for both; at N=24 each uses 4 beams with `3+7+7+7`. Over the full sweep the optimum varies with the integer remainder and ACM steps, rather than collapsing to either corner. If every beam is forced onto a distinct satellite, the extra 0.200 W per beam changes only SEALED N=9 (`4+5` to `9`) and N=24 (`3+7+7+7` to `8+8+8`), and MARGIN N=24 (`3+7+7+7` to `8+8+8`) at this geometry; all other N partitions are unchanged."
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:422:        "The grid spans boresight, half-radius, and the 1.66 deg beam edge, with 500/750/1000 km slants; elevation is held at 30 deg so this isolates the two requested axes and keeps q10 fixed. These are analytic link inputs, not assertions that every angle/range pair is one orbital state. Each cell below repeats the N=24 optimization; the script also repeats every N=1..24 cell when producing the change counts."
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:428:        f"Against the reference-geometry partition at the same N, SEALED changes in {sealed_geo[0]} of {sealed_geo[1]} grid-by-N comparisons and MARGIN changes in {margin_geo[0]} of {margin_geo[1]}. "
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:429:        f"Holding slant fixed and moving off boresight changes SEALED in {sealed_angle[0]}/{sealed_angle[1]} comparisons (maximum active-beam change {sealed_angle[2]}) and MARGIN in {margin_angle[0]}/{margin_angle[1]} (maximum {margin_angle[2]}). Holding angle fixed and increasing range changes SEALED in {sealed_range[0]}/{sealed_range[1]} comparisons (maximum {sealed_range[2]}) and MARGIN in {margin_range[0]}/{margin_range[1]} (maximum {margin_range[2]}). "
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:430:        f"Across the grid and N sweep, SEALED uses {sealed_geo[2]}..{sealed_geo[3]} active beams and MARGIN uses {margin_geo[2]}..{margin_geo[3]}; singleton populations force the lower endpoint. At N=24 the grid spans 3..4 beams for SEALED and 3..5 for MARGIN, while feasible maximum occupancy spans 7..12 and 5..12 respectively. Therefore the optimum is not geometry-invariant: both angle and range can be decision-relevant through PA/fixed-cost scaling and cap feasibility, even without interference."
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:440:        f"The interior optimum survives. At N=24, SEALED remains `{partition_text(sealed_zero_n24.partition)}` and MARGIN remains `{partition_text(margin_zero_n24.partition)}` after fixed costs are removed; neither becomes one beam or 24 singleton beams. The zero-fixed-cost partitions are identical between SEALED and MARGIN because MARGIN multiplies every feasible RF requirement by the same 1/q10 at fixed elevation, and the square-root PA law therefore multiplies every beam's supply by the same `1/sqrt(q10)`. The discriminator says the interior is driven by discrete mode/capacity thresholds plus the PA law; fixed costs shift the selected mix at other N but do not create the interior."
scripts/run_occupancy_convexity.py:451:    add("The program prints this report. It imports the production ACM, antenna/noise, nominal-path, PA-supply, and authenticated q10 functions; exhaustive integer partition enumeration is local diagnostic logic. No sealed artifact is modified.")
